<reference id="_Toc238560414" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Scenario 3: Code block inside a procedure</title>
   <shortdesc>Consider a procedure where a command must be executed during a step.</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>block</keyword>
        <keyword>procedure</keyword>
        <keyword>deployment</keyword>
        <keyword>Code</keyword>
        <keyword>inside</keyword>
        <keyword>command</keyword>
        <indexterm>block</indexterm>
        <indexterm>procedure</indexterm>
        <indexterm>deployment</indexterm>
      </keywords>
      <prodinfo>
        <prodname/>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <refbody>  <section>
    <p>Consider a procedure where a command must be executed during a step.</p><table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
            <title>Code block inside a procedure</title>
            <tgroup cols="2">
               <colspec colname="c1"/>
               <colspec colname="c2"/>
              <thead>
                <row>
                  <entry> .md input </entry>
                  <entry> DITA output </entry>
                </row>                
              </thead>
               <tbody>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                       <codeblock>1. Run the following command:
                         
                         ```bash
                         kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml
                         ```
                         
                         2. Verify the deployment
                       </codeblock>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                       <codeblock>&lt;steps&gt;
                         &lt;step&gt;
                         &lt;cmd&gt;
                         Run the following command:
                         &lt;/cmd&gt;
                         &lt;info&gt;
                         &lt;codeblock outputclass="bash"&gt;
                         kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml
                         &lt;/codeblock&gt;
                         &lt;/info&gt;
                         &lt;/step&gt;
                         &lt;step&gt;
                         &lt;cmd&gt;Verify the deployment.&lt;/cmd&gt;
                         &lt;/step&gt;
                         &lt;/steps&gt;
                       </codeblock>
  </entry>
  </row>
  </tbody></tgroup>
                     </table>
      <p><b>Result:</b> The converter associates the code block with the preceding procedural step
        and places it within the corresponding <codeph>&lt;info&gt;</codeph> element.</p>
  </section></refbody>
</reference>
